      "problem": "Find $k$ if $6$ is a root of $f(x)=8{x}^{3}-46{x}^{2}-26kx+6.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since  $x=6$ is a root, we have $f(6)=0.$ Therefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=6,$ set it equal to $0,$ and solve the equation for the parameter $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8(6)^{3}-46(6)^{2}-26k(6)+6 & =0 \\\\ 1\\,728-1\\,656-156k+6 & =0 \\\\ 78-156k & =0 \\\\ -156k & =-78 \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
